      "text": "Breakfast in a hotel. \n\nCholula Tour, watched over by the Popocatepetl and the Iztaccihuatl grew up one of the great cities of the pre-Hispanic world, known for its iconic pyramid which has the title of being the largest pyramid base in the world with 450 meters on each side, The pyramid is a temple that was traditionally considered to be dedicated to the god Quetzalcoatl. \n\nWe continue to Huaquechula, a nearby town, where the celebration in honor of the deceased is unique and colorful. One of the highlights is the altars, which are usually decorated with flowers, candles, photographs, food, and personal belongings of each deceased. \n\nAfterwards return to Puebla, we will have the opportunity to discover a city that perfectly combines its rich heritage with a modern spirit. We'll walk through its cobbled streets and lively squares. \n\nThe tour begins in the heart of Puebla: in the Zócalo and the Cathedral, declared a World Heritage Site by UNESCO, we will also discover the Chapel of the Rosary, a masterpiece of the Baroque considered one of the most ornate in America. "
    },
